EXT. SHELLED VILLAGE - CELLAR HATCH - NIGHT

Broken roofs. A church tower snapped in half. Flares drift down on parachutes and the ground shudders with distant guns.

CORPORAL YUSUF DEMIR, thirties, crouches at a cellar hatch with a rifle across his knees. Beside him lies PRIVATE HALLORAN "HAL" QUIST, nineteen, on his back, helmet over his eyes.

Yusuf shoves him.

YUSUF
Up.

HAL
I am up.

YUSUF
You're lying down.

HAL
It's a different kind of up.

A shell lands close. Dirt rains. Both flatten. The ringing fades.

YUSUF
Count.

HAL
One. Two.

YUSUF
Not shells. Us.

HAL
Two.

Yusuf nods. He rises to a crouch and peers over the ruined wall. A flare dies. Darkness.

YUSUF
We go on three.

HAL
Where?

YUSUF
The bridge.

HAL
There is no bridge.

YUSUF
There's a bridge.

HAL
There was a bridge.

Yusuf looks at him. Hal sits up and pushes his helmet back.

YUSUF
Hal.

HAL
I know.

YUSUF
If I say go, you go.

HAL
I know.

YUSUF
If I fall, you keep going.

HAL
I know.

YUSUF ^
One.

HAL
(at the same time)
One.

They exchange a glance. A flare pops overhead and the night turns white.

YUSUF
Two.

Hal checks his rifle. Yusuf takes a breath.

YUSUF (CONT'D)
Three.

They run.
